  "interpretation": [
    "NG200 improves the measured one-period recurrence relative to NG48, but two meshes with changed timestep/backend are not a standalone spatial-order estimate.",
    "The original random realization was not supplied; these are seeded protocol reproductions, not pointwise copies of the published panels.",
    "Legacy viscosity depends on grid scale and evolving flow strength. NG48 and NG200 therefore do not hold the physical viscosity coefficient fixed; their damping difference is not a fixed-viscosity convergence test.",
    "Energy and PV-enstrophy budget drift are distinguished from relative-enstrophy change and angular-momentum leakage.",
    "These one-period wave controls do not establish a long-time turbulent end state."
  ]
